{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Lateralus feels like a natural next choice because my recent interest in 10.000 Days makes me want to explore more Tool.",
    "Master of Puppets and The End of Heartache match the aggressive riffs and blend of melody and heaviness I have been seeking in Advance And Vanquish, In Flames, and Soilwork; Korn also fits the heavy grooves I enjoyed in Ten Thousand Fists."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Encore does not give me the heavy guitar sound I want now, and my recent listening gives me little reason to reach for rap.",
    "Room for Squares feels too soft for my current mood. The Open Door and Fallen are closer, but their melodic rock appeal does not make them as compelling today as the heavier albums I chose."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My earlier interest in accessible rock seems to have been carried too far into softer music, overlooking how much heavier my recent choices have become.",
    "Sharing an artist is not enough to make two albums equally appealing: I would choose Master of Puppets over St. Anger because its riffs better fit what I want today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest Tool and Disturbed listening matters to my immediate mood, especially the pull toward immersive songs and heavy grooves.",
    "My repeated In Flames listening alongside Soilwork points to a particular balance of melody and aggression, which makes The End of Heartache especially appealing rather than just any rock album."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The choices mostly recognize my interest in heavy music, but sometimes stretch my broader rock history beyond the sounds I want right now."
}"}
